    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIEm">III Em</ref> 7.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="191" ed="#liebermann"/>Et omnes infamati<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#IIIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.a"/> et accusationibus ingrauati sub plegio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#missing"/> redigantur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="14" ed="#robertson"/>Et omnes infamati et accusationibus ingravati sub plegio redigantur.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIIEm_7-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="15" ed="#robertson"/>And all men of ill repute and those who have been frequently accused<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIIEm_7-1.robnote.n.2"/> shall be placed under surety.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="191"><ref target="clause:IIAs_20-1">II As 20.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:IIAs_20-4">II As 20.4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As. 20, 1. 4</note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann. Liebermann compares II As 20, 1.4.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ <hi rend="italic">ealle þa ungetriewan</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">tyhtbysigan</hi> [<hi rend="italic">men?</hi>] <hi rend="italic">man gebrenge under borge</hi> las Or. laut I Atr 1, 1. 4; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Bescholtene 2—4; Bürgschaft 6g. i. Von allgemeiner Freibürgschaft ist noch keine Rede; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Zehnerschaft 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ <hi rend="italic">ealle þa ungetriewan</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">tyhtbysigan</hi> [<hi rend="italic">men?</hi>] <hi rend="italic">man gebrenge under borge</hi> was the reading of the original, according to I Atr 1, 1. 4; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Bescholtene 2—4; Bürgschaft 6g. i. There is as yet no question of general frankpledge; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Zehnerschaft 9</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIEm_7-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II As. 20, 1 and 4.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIEm_7-1.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann suggests that the A.S. text read <hi rend="italic">þa ungetriewan</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">tyhtbysigan</hi> (<hi rend="italic">men?</hi>), cf. III Edg. 7; I Atr. 1, 1; 4; II Cn. 25; 30.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
